Zone-scaled creatures defend at their effective (displayed) level, not their real one.

Touches: src/server/game/Entities/Creature/Creature.cpp,
Creature::getLevelForTarget()

Why: reports #88/#89 -- a level 7 in Shadowglen could not land hits on
zone-scaled mobs. Zone scaling (LivingGear module) is deliberately
display-and-damage-only: UNIT_FIELD_LEVEL keeps the mob's REAL level so the
shared health bar never desyncs between viewers, and the damage exchanged is
rescaled per viewer by LivingGear_Perks. But the engine's spell-hit roll
(Spell::CheckHit -> Unit::MagicSpellHitResult) computes levelDiff from
victim->getLevelForTarget(attacker), which for a creature is its real level.
An effective-8 mob whose real level is 80 therefore carries +72 levels of
spell-miss, and melee suffers the same through GetMaxSkillValueForLevel /
GetDefenseSkillValue (both level*5) -- the module now corrects those numbers
at roll time via OnBeforeRollMeleeOutcomeAgainst, but spells read this
function directly and no script hook reaches it.

The override asks the Living Gear module what level this creature presents
to THIS attacker and answers with that, keeping every hit-roll consumer --
spells, and any future reader of getLevelForTarget -- consistent with what
the player sees on the target frame. The module exposes
LivingGear_CombatLevelFor(Creature*, Player*), which returns 0 when zone
scaling does not apply to the pair; in that case the stock behaviour stands.
Weak-linkage via a plain extern function would drag the module into the core
link, so the hook is a ScriptMgr call instead:
sScriptMgr->OnCreatureGetLevelForTarget(const Creature*, const WorldObject*,
uint8&) with a default no-op in UnitScript.

Applies only to non-world-boss creatures (world bosses already scale to the
target in the stock code path below).
--- a/src/server/game/Scripting/ScriptDefines/UnitScript.h
+++ b/src/server/game/Scripting/ScriptDefines/UnitScript.h
@@ -107,6 +107,9 @@
     virtual void OnUnitEnterCombat(Unit* /*unit*/, Unit* /*victim*/) { }
     virtual void OnUnitExitCombat(Unit* /*unit*/) { }
+    // Living Gear zone scaling (#88/#89): let the module answer "what level
+    // does this creature fight at against this viewer". outLevel defaults to
+    // the creature's real level; a module may overwrite it per-viewer.
+    virtual void OnCreatureLevelForTarget(Unit const* /*creature*/, WorldObject const* /*target*/, uint8& /*outLevel*/) { }

--- a/src/server/game/Scripting/ScriptMgr.h
+++ b/src/server/game/Scripting/ScriptMgr.h
@@ (near OnBeforeRollMeleeOutcomeAgainst)
+    void OnCreatureLevelForTarget(Unit const* creature, WorldObject const* target, uint8& outLevel);

--- a/src/server/game/Scripting/ScriptMgr.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Scripting/ScriptMgr.cpp
@@ (alongside the other UnitScript forwards)
+void ScriptMgr::OnCreatureLevelForTarget(Unit const* creature, WorldObject const* target, uint8& outLevel)
+{
+    FOREACH_SCRIPT(UnitScript)->OnCreatureLevelForTarget(creature, target, outLevel);
+}

--- a/src/server/game/Entities/Creature/Creature.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Entities/Creature/Creature.cpp
@@ Creature::getLevelForTarget
 uint8 Creature::getLevelForTarget(WorldObject const* target) const
 {
     if (!isWorldBoss() || !target->ToUnit())
-        return Unit::getLevelForTarget(target);
+    {
+        uint8 level = Unit::getLevelForTarget(target);
+        sScriptMgr->OnCreatureLevelForTarget(this, target, level);
+        return level;
+    }
